%N A400368 Nonsquarefree numbers k such that sigma(k) = phi(k) + tau(k)^7.
%C A400368 All squarefree numbers k such that sigma(k) = phi(k) + tau(k)^7 are terms of the sequence A398648.
%H A400368 David A. Corneth, <a href="/A400368/b400368.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..24</a> (terms <= 10^15)
%H A400368 David A. Corneth, <a href="/A400368/a400368.gp.txt">Some more terms with possible gaps in between</a>
%H A400368 S. I. Dimitrov, <a href="https://github.com/Stoyan16/Non-squarefree-numbers-k-such-that-sigma-k-phi-k-tau-k-7/blob/main/A400368">Python program</a> (GitHub)
%e A400368 1194649 is a term since sigma(1194649) = 1195743 = 1193556 + 3^7 = phi(1194649) + tau(1194649)^7.
%o A400368 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); !issquarefree(f) && sigma(f) - eulerphi(f) == numdiv(f)^7; } \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 24 2026
%Y A400368 Cf. A000005, A000010, A000203, A013929, A398648, A399944, A399226.
%K A400368 nonn,hard,new
